WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:29.620
[Music]

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.200
[Narrator:] Here is the house where mercy dwells and walks in white shoes

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.933
softly down the corridors of pain.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:41.466
Only yesterday, those corridors were thronged like this with nurses,

00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:45.099
whole platoons of nurses, graduate and practical,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.900
paid and volunteer aides, bringing their competence and sympathy

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.000
to the suffering and the sick.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.366
But that was yesterday.  Today with more people than ever before seeking

00:00:56.366 --> 00:01:00.899
medical attention, with more patients than beds in hospitals,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.533
and only 300,000 registered graduate nurses on active service,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.160
our nation faces a grave and immediate crisis.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.733
The lights on the hospital call-board flash faster today than they can be answered.

00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:25.299
Each one is a distress signal sent to thousands of nurses who aren't there, who don't exist.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:30.933
[Music]

00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:36.999
But here are three who will answer, three out of the 43,000 American girls

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.333
who, very determined and probably a little frightened, are entering nursing school this year.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.300
Let's follow one of them, Betty Burns,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:53.280
as she starts out on the climb that will take her across the threshold of a new and exciting life,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.480
the profession and the privilege of serving humanity.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:04.233
Now, for a nervous neophyte like Betty, there is pleasure and relief at the warmth of her greeting.

00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:12.166
This is more than simple kindness. Much of it is in the appreciation of graduates and other students that their ranks must be kept filled,

00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:16.732
that today, at least, there cannot be too many new nurses.

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:21.766
After the handshakes and the smiles, though, Betty has to go through registration,

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:26.299
must get her copy of the schedule, her first reminder of the work she will complete

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.233
before she can serve those who may someday need her.

00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:35.233
There are books and supplies to crowd her first exciting day,

00:02:35.233 --> 00:02:40.766
such basic studies as chemistry and others essential to an understanding of medicine.

00:02:40.766 --> 00:02:45.260
And Betty learns that there are emotions in almost every beaker.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.660
And no sooner has one class ended than it's time for the next,

00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:52.566
this one: Anatomy, without which you cannot

00:02:52.566 --> 00:02:56.080
understand or make yourself understood in medicine.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.300
There are the precise instruments of microbiology,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:10.660
an introduction to crime detection and the underworld of man's almost invisible enemies.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.133
Betty learns that taking a census of deadly organisms

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:20.266
could scarcely be learned at home and that cooking becomes a potent tool

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.760
of healing under the name nutrition and diet therapy.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:34.300
And soon, she'll have a student nurse uniform, will look so much like a nurse that she'll almost feel like one.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.666
See?  Now, she's the pride of her nursing arts class, even though her patient,

00:03:42.666 --> 00:03:47.532
Mary Chase, shows slight appreciation of her attention.

00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:52.133
Here again, Betty finds that scores of simple things she did at home must be practiced

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:54.899
with proper hospital precision.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:01.900
All this concentration, however, is destined to make instinctive the hundreds of details in the work she is preparing for.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.780
The habits of care and exactness may someday ease a suffering patient.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.500
After months of preclinical work comes a great occasion,

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.700
the capping ceremony, when Betty and her successful classmates

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.633
will be rewarded with the distinctive cap of their hospital.

00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:29.999
Once she has the cap, she knows she's passed the stiff requirements.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.333
The emotional satisfaction is deep, for this milestone

00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:38.933
is marked by ceremonial flames commemorating nursing's great mentor,

00:04:38.933 --> 00:04:40.433
Florence Nightingale,

00:04:40.433 --> 00:04:42.833
"the Lady with the Lamp."

00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:47.366
Veneration of a great tradition means much to these young student nurses,

00:04:47.366 --> 00:04:50.632
and perhaps the cap means more.

00:04:50.633 --> 00:04:52.333
Men may not understand this.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.860
Women will.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:00.860
Betty starts clinical training by preparing a medication.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.133
Her exactness and her careful check of each detail in the delicate matter of dosage

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.633
are more important than mere steps in a severe routine.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.160
Precision here is an absolutely necessary factor in the successful treatment

00:05:14.166 --> 00:05:18.366
of a patient who will soon receive this medicine, and the correct performance

00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:22.699
of Betty's job is watched by an experienced graduate nurse instructor.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.260
A human life may someday depend on her precision.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.833
Treatment trays and those everlasting forceps.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.560
You'd almost think they'd find a simpler way to keep instruments sterile.

00:05:37.566 --> 00:05:43.699
But you'll learn, Miss Burns. You will learn by doing, and you'll get so that it's second nature

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.740
to baffle the bacteria.

00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:54.660
And here, as everywhere, accuracy, forethought, and speed.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.940
No time to waste but no excuse for error.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:04.933
The doctor who will use this tray cannot take the time to hunt for any items you might forget.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.733
By knowing that they are all in order and by getting them to him promptly,

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.460
you have helped him in his vital work.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:24.160
Getting the right things to the right places on time is of prime importance in any organized activity,

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.680
especially in the work of caring for the sick.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.233
Unless you have been accompanied by a graduate nurse,

00:06:32.233 --> 00:06:36.166
you could not have left that tray of medicine to help move this patient.

00:06:36.166 --> 00:06:39.140
Your skill makes this an easy task.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:59.060
[Music]

00:06:59.066 --> 00:07:01.499
Now that medicine, remember?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.333
Well, here's a third change, this one in two steps.

00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:07.766
First, ask the patient her name.

00:07:07.766 --> 00:07:12.620
Then, compare the card with this official one to make doubly sure.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:20.360
You learn which patient likes which kind of bedside manner.

00:07:20.366 --> 00:07:23.999
And you find that knowing how to keep on pleasant, easy terms

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.866
with the sick makes your task simpler and helps speed their cures as well.

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:35.120
Often, they'll reward you with a smile of thanks, which makes this work worthwhile.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.033
Many phases of hospital work are so highly technical

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.699
that nurses must be ready to help their doctors

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.780
in an almost endless variety of complex treatments.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:48.960
The Balkan frame, often seen in orthopedic wards,

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.000
is a challenge to those charged with speeding a patient's recovery.

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:05.399
Of course, all work and no play will make Betty a dull girl.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:10.533
But here, fun, like work, is strictly conditioned by that old devil, time.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:17.333
It made you almost as quick in putting on your party clothes as you are with your uniform.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:22.800
But because the heavy date must impressed, you take extra special care.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:28.100
He's just starting out on his career, too, and any economies are helpful.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:40.200
So those flowers you got from that generous patient in maternity this afternoon

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.966
will help out in this evening's serious financial problems

00:08:43.966 --> 00:08:47.680
But you kept them fresh in the tray room icebox.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:55.400
This is one occasion, Miss Burns, when you can indulge

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.033
in the luxury of making someone wait.

00:08:58.033 --> 00:09:02.566
Here, for a few blissful moments, you are privileged to play a commanding role.

00:09:02.566 --> 00:09:06.060
You can, if you want, even forget tomorrow's assignment in the clinic.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:18.360
[Music]

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.000
But you can't forget for long.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.933
And you've learned that there's a clock in every good nurse's subconscious mind.

00:09:24.933 --> 00:09:28.499
So make the goodbye short and sweet, and hurry back.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:35.766
Tomorrow is another day, a day with outpatients and the versatile hospital personnel which cares for them.

00:09:35.766 --> 00:09:38.720
Only experienced students are qualified here,

00:09:39.466 --> 00:09:44.020
and the black stripe on Betty's cap shows that she has over two years of work behind her.

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:48.499
Her cases are so varied that she will find use for everything she's learned.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:54.066
Her hospital moves out into her community, expanding its service to every citizen.

00:09:54.066 --> 00:09:58.599
This work gives scope for almost all the knowledge a nurse can get.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:04.800
Luckily, Betty's background is now wide, and since her tastes run toward pediatric nursing,

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.960
caring for this young patient is a gratifying experience.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:25.800
[Music]

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:33.000
Training is like the job itself, an accumulation of habits and skills learned from each one.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.333
Accuracy in time, in temperature, deftness in every movement of the hands,

00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:42.666
a constant determination that no bacterial invaders can be allowed.

00:10:42.666 --> 00:10:49.060
It takes all these skills and more to qualify for surgery, where technical perfection is idolized.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:58.633
So highly trained and coordinated are the hands and mind of this member of the surgical team,

00:10:58.633 --> 00:11:01.166
she is eloquently termed the scrub nurse,

00:11:01.166 --> 00:11:03.932
that they provide, as a matter of course,

00:11:03.933 --> 00:11:06.699
the right instruments at the right instant.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:11.600
It's as if there were a link between her hands and the surgeon's brain.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:20.133
If there were not, if these lightning fingers faltered, their failure might spell death beneath that sterile sheet.

00:11:20.133 --> 00:11:36.466
[Dramatic music]

00:11:36.466 --> 00:11:40.032
The strain of an operation is almost overpowering.

00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:44.466
But the patient is okay, and Betty knows that she did well.

00:11:44.466 --> 00:11:48.320
Even so, she's glad the supervisor thinks so, too.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:55.433
The human touch is everywhere when you serve humanity,

00:11:55.433 --> 00:11:59.766
and perhaps this is most keenly felt in the obstetrical nursery.

00:11:59.766 --> 00:12:03.766
Here, a stern aseptic discipline keeps even parents out.

00:12:03.766 --> 00:12:06.799
But Mr. Clarke, the father, can present his card.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:14.580
And Betty, all swathed in sterile clothes, will see if Girl Clarke cares to interview the gentleman through the window.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:22.800
[Music]

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.833
Well, Miss Burns, it looks as if you've hit the jackpot.

00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:32.333
You've reached pediatric training, at last.  And what a thrill to be among these appreciative youngsters.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.060
It's the kind of work you've always wanted.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:43.760
[Music]

00:12:43.766 --> 00:12:47.966
You've come to the end of the beginning: graduation,

00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:52.432
that goal through years of stern study and patient practice.

00:12:52.433 --> 00:12:57.999
You're thinking of the oath first sworn by that immortal of your sisterhood,

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.633
Florence Nightingale.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:06.233
"I solemnly pledge myself before God to practice my profession faithfully,

00:13:06.233 --> 00:13:09.433
to elevate the standard of my profession

00:13:09.433 --> 00:13:15.699
and hold in confidence all personal matters committed to my keeping.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:19.466
With loyalty will I endeavor to aid the physician in his work

00:13:19.466 --> 00:13:24.799
and devote myself to the welfare of those committed to my care."

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:33.966
[Music]

00:13:33.966 --> 00:13:40.199
This is it, Betty. Now you're one of this year's 34,000 new graduate nurses.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.833
What lies ahead for these girls in white?

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.360
[Henry J. Vier, M.D.]  Well, here's your classmate, Mary Ballard,

00:13:48.366 --> 00:13:51.599
typical of thousands who help doctors and office nurses.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.600
Her counseling and placement service told her she'd be well suited to this work.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.780
And Mary's boss and hundreds of patients are glad they did.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.833
Then there's Jane Gillespie.  She chose a public health career.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.680
She's bringing nursing to people who cannot get to hospital.

00:14:13.766 --> 00:14:17.260
Each will go where she is needed most, no matter where,

00:14:17.266 --> 00:14:21.599
like Lieutenant Katie Moore, on duty at an army hospital here,

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.900
awaiting orders to Yokohama.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:29.700
And you, Miss Burns, you are in a hospital at night,

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.733
you and your little patients.  And it's a Saturday,

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:38.140
no date, just you and... But what's that noise?

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.333
You're lucky for your training, Betty Burns.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:48.820
You know that this is not the major emergency in this nerve-wracked group.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:15:02.433
This is. You, like thousands of your sister nurses in hospital staff assignments, have learned to gauge an emergency.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:07.820
It's well you have. You may have saved a life because you know your job.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:13.933
The general practice of nursing has come a long way down the corridors of time

00:15:13.933 --> 00:15:17.033
since this nurse assisted at her first operation.

00:15:17.033 --> 00:15:20.566
She has seen a hundred changes in practice and procedure.

00:15:20.566 --> 00:15:25.999
But Nightingale's lamp burned brightly in her heart way back when she graduated,

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.000
starched and proud and inspired by the ideal of service.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:37.740
That flame is still bright and clear and rekindles itself in each succeeding class of incoming students.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:43.800
[Music]

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:52.380
Yes, look well at Betty Burns, registered nurse, handmaiden to the noblest art of man, healing.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.433
With skill and stamina, with courage and compassion,

00:15:56.433 --> 00:16:00.199
she is dedicated to the service of suffering humanity.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:04.200
Hers is a profession and a privilege.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.880
Yes, say it proudly, and you need no further definition.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.540
She is a nurse.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:16.900
[Music]

